h \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 No, my goodness, not at all. And that\uc1 \u8217 ?s the reason there were worse teachers than me\uc1 \u8212 ?those who believed they understood something. At least I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t ruin the judgment or the hands of the children. When they left me for a good teacher, they\uc1 \u8217 ?d learned nothing, and so at least they didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t have to unlearn anything. And that was always so much time and money saved.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 How did you manage that?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 How they all do. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d get there and throw myself into a chair. \uc1 \u8220 ?What dreadful weather! How tiring the pavement is!\uc1 \u8221 ? I would chatter about some news: \uc1 \u8220 ?Mademoiselle Lemierre was to have taken on the role of a vestal virgin in the new opera. But she is pregnant for the second time. They don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know who will take her place. Mademoiselle Arnould has just left her little count. People say she is negotiating with Bertin. The little count, however, has just found the secret of Monsieur de Montamy\uc1 \u8217 ?s porcelain. At the last concert for the lovers of music there was an Italian woman who sang like an angel. That Pr\uc1 \u233 ?ville is an exceptional fellow.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Lemierre and Arnould were singers, and Preville a well known actor. De Montamy, a colleague of Diderot, tried to make Chinese porcelain. }}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  You must see him in }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Le Mercure galant}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 . The part about the riddle is priceless. And poor Dumesnil no longer knows what she\uc1 \u8217 ?s saying or doing. Come, Mademoiselle, take your book.\uc1 \u8221 ? While the young lady, who\uc1 \u8217 ?s in no hurry, looks for her book, which she has mislaid, and while the maid is being summoned and chastised, I keep going, \uc1 \u8220 ?That Clairon is truly incomprehensible. People are talking about a really crazy marriage\uc1 \u8212 ?one with Mademoiselle What\uc1 \u8217 ?s-Her-Name, a little creature he\uc1 \u8217 ?s been supporting, with whom he\uc1 \u8217 ?s had two or three }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 children,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  and who\uc1 \u8217 ?s been kept by so many others.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Come now, Rameau, that\uc1 \u8217 ?s not possible. You\uc1 \u8217 ?re rambling on.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?No, I\uc1 \u8217 ?m not rambling. They even say that the marriage has taken place. There\uc1 \u8217 ?s a rumour going around that Voltaire is dead. So much the better.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Why\uc1 \u8217 ?s that good?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Well, that means he\uc1 \u8217 ?s going to give us some fine foolishness. He has a habit of dying two weeks before he does so.\uc1 \u8221 ? What else shall I tell you? I\uc1 \u8217 ?d mention to her a few naughty remarks which I brought back from some homes where I\uc1 \u8217 ?d been, for we are all great gossips. I played the fool, and they listened to me. They laughed. They\uc1 \u8217 ?d cry out, \uc1 \u8220 ?He\uc1 \u8217 ?s always charming.\uc1 \u8221 ? However, the young lady\uc1 \u8217 ?s book would finally be recovered from under an armchair, where it had been dragged, chewed, and ripped by a young pug dog or a kitten. She\uc1 \u8217 ?d sit at the keyboard. At first she would make some noise there, all by herself. Then I\uc1 \u8217 ?d come up, having given her mother a sign of approval. The mother would say, \uc1 \u8220 ?That isn\uc1 \u8217 ?t bad. One only needs to want to do it, but she doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t want to. She prefers to waste her time with chit-chat, clothes, running around, and I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know what. As soon as you\uc1 \u8217 ?re gone, the book is closed, and it\uc1 \u8217 ?s not opened again until you return. And then you never reprimand her . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? However, since I would have to do something, I\uc1 \u8217 ?d take her hands and place them in a different position. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d get upset. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d cry out, \uc1 \u8220 ?G, G, G, Mademoiselle. It\uc1 \u8217 ?s a G.\uc1 \u8221 ? The mother, \uc1 \u8220 ?Young lady, don\uc1 \u8217 ?t you have an ear? I\uc1 \u8217 ?m not even at the keyboard, and I\uc1 \u8217 ?m not looking at your book, but I feel that must be a G. You\uc1 \u8217 ?re giving this gentleman a great deal of trouble. I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t understand his patience. You don\uc1 \u8217 ?t retain anything he tells you. You\uc1 \u8217 ?re not progressing at all . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? Then I would ease the blows a little by shaking my head and saying, \uc1 \u8220 ?Excuse me, Madame, excuse me. Yes, that could go better, if the young lady wanted to, if she studied a little. But it\uc1 \u8217 ?s not going badly.\uc1 \u8221 ? The mother: \uc1 \u8220 ?In your place, I\uc1 \u8217 ?d keep her on the same piece for a year.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?That\uc1 \u8217 ?s all right\uc1 \u8212 ?she won\uc1 \u8217 ?t leave it until she has surmounted all the difficulties, and that won\uc1 \u8217 ?t take as long as Madam thinks.\uc1 \u8221 ? The mother: \uc1 \u8220 ?Monsieur Rameau, you\uc1 \u8217 ?re flattering her. You\uc1 \u8217 ?re too kind. That\uc1 \u8217 ?s the only thing she\uc1 \u8217 ?ll remember from her lesson, and she\uc1 \u8217 ?ll know the right time to repeat it in front of me.\uc1 \u8221 ? The hour went by. My pupil would give me the small fee, with a graceful movement of her arm and the curtsy she had learned from her dancing master. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d put it in my pocket, while the mother said, \uc1 \u8220 ?Very good, Mademoiselle. If Javillier were here, he\uc1 \u8217 ?d applaud you}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 .}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8221 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Jacques Javillier was a well known dancer and dancing master.}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025   I\uc1 \u8217 ?d keep chatting for a moment longer out of courtesy and then disappear. There you have it\uc1 \u8212 ?that\uc1 \u8217 ?s what people used to call a lesson in accompaniment in those days.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 And nowadays, it\uc1 \u8217 ?s something different?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rt