?raire}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 L}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8217 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Observateur litt\uc1 \u233 ?raire}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8212 ?that\uc1 \u8217 ?s not possible. They detest each other.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 That\uc1 \u8217 ?s true. But all beggars are reconciled at the feeding trough. That damned }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Observateur litt\uc1 \u233 ?raire}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8212 ?I wish the devil had taken the man and his columns. It\uc1 \u8217 ?s that little cur of an avaricious priest, that stinking usurer, who\uc1 \u8217 ?s the cause of my disaster. He appeared on our horizon for the first time yesterday. He arrived at the hour which drives us all out of our hideouts\uc1 \u8212 ?dinner time. When the weather is bad, anyone among us who has a twenty-four-sou coin in his pocket is a happy man. There are some who made fun of a fellow beggar who arrived in the morning with mud up to his ribs and soaked to the bone who in the evening returned to their homes in the same condition. There was one of them\uc1 \u8212 ?I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know which one\uc1 \u8212 ?who a few months ago had a violent tangle with the Savoyard who had set up at our door. They were running on credit, and the creditor wanted the debtor to settle up, but the latter didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t have the money. Well, they serve the meal and honour the Abb\uc1 \u233 ? by placing him at the head of the table. I come in. I notice him. So I say to him, \uc1 \u8220 ?Well, Abb\uc1 \u233 ?, so you\uc1 \u8217 ?re presiding today? That\uc1 \u8217 ?s fine for today, but tomorrow you move down one setting, if you please, and the day after tomorrow to the next place setting, and thus from place to place, either to the left or right, until you move from that place which I\uc1 \u8217 ?ve occupied once before you, Fr\uc1 \u233 ?ron once after me, Dorat once after Fr\uc1 \u233 ?ron, Palissot once after Dorat, and come to rest beside me, a poor dull bugger like yourself, }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 q}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ui siedo sempre come un maestoso cazzo fra duoi coglioni [who always sits here like a majestic prick between two balls]}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 . The Abb\uc1 \u233 ?, who\uc1 \u8217 ?s a good little devil and takes everything well, began to laugh. Mademoiselle was struck by the truth of my observation and the justness of my comparison, and she began to laugh. All those who were seated to the right and to the left of the Abb\uc1 \u233 ? and whom he had moved down one notch began to laugh. Everyone was laughing except Monsieur who was irritated and went at me with things which wouldn\uc1 \u8217 ?t have mattered at all if we\uc1 \u8217 ?d been alone: \uc1 \u8220 ?Rameau you\uc1 \u8217 ?re an impudent man.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I know that\uc1 \u8212 ?that\uc1 \u8217 ?s why you receive me here.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?A scoundrel.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Just like the others.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?A beggar.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Would I be here if I weren\uc1 \u8217 ?t?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll see to it that you\uc1 \u8217 ?re thrown out.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?After dinner, I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll leave on my own.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I\uc1 \u8217 ?d advise you to do that.\uc1 \u8221 ? So we ate, and I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t miss a bite. After we\uc1 \u8217 ?d eaten well and drunk a good deal, because, after all, it wouldn\uc1 \u8217 ?t have mattered one way or the other\uc1 \u8212 ?Monsieur Belly is not someone I've ever refused to have anything to do with\uc1 \u8212 ?I made my decision and was preparing to leave. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d given my word in the presence of so many people that I had to keep it. I was prowling around the apartment for a long time, looking for my walking stick and my hat in places where they wouldn\uc1 \u8217 ?t be, all the time counting on the fact that my patron would let out a new torrent of abuse, someone would intervene, and we\uc1 \u8217 ?d finish up by being reconciled because we\uc1 \u8217 ?d lost our tempers. I wandered around, I kept wandering around, for I wasn\uc1 \u8217 ?t feeling anything inside. But my patron, well, he was blacker and grimmer than Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s Apollo when he fired his arrows down on the Greek army. He was walking back and forth, with his cap pulled down more than usual and his fist under his chin. Mademoiselle came up to me. \uc1 \u8220 ?But Mademoiselle, what\uc1 \u8217 ?s been so extraordinary, then? Have I been any different today from my usual self?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I wish him to leave.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I will leave. I haven\uc1 \u8217 ?t wronged him in any way.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Excuse me, but Monsieur l\uc1 \u8217 ?Abb\uc1 \u233 ? was invited, and . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?He let himself down by inviting the Abb\uc1 \u233 ? and then letting me in and with me so many other hangers-on like me.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Come on, my dear Rameau. You must apologize to Monsieur l\uc1 \u8217 ?Abb\uc1 \u233 ?.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t want his pardon . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Come on, come on\uc1 \u8212 ?all this will sort itself out.\uc1 \u8221 ? They take me by the hand and drag me towards the Abb\uc1 \u233 ?\uc1 \u8217 ?s armchair. I hold out my arms. I look at the Abb\uc1 \u233 ? with a sort of admiration, for who has ever asked the Abb\uc1 \u233 ? to pardon him? \uc1 \u8220 ?Abb\uc1 \u233 ?,\uc1 \u8221 ? I say to him, \uc1 \u8220 ?Abb\uc1 \u233 ?, all this is really silly, isn\uc1 \u8217 ?t it?\uc1 \u8221 ? And then I start to laugh, and so does he. So right there I was forgiven in that quarter. But I had to tackle the other one, and what I had to say to him was a different game altogether. I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know much about how I framed my apology. \uc1 \u8220 ?Monsieur, look at this fool . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?He\uc1 \u8217 ?s been making me suffer for too long. I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t want to hear any more talk about him.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Monsieur is angry.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Yes, I am very angry.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?That won\uc1 \u8217 ?t happen to him anymore.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Well, the first scoundrel . . .\uc1 \u8221 ? I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know if he was in one of his moody days when Mademoiselle is afraid to go near him and doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t dare touch him except with velvet }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 mitts,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  or whether he misheard what I was }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 saying,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  or whether I spoke badly, but things got worse than before. To hell with it\uc1 \u8212 ?doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t he know me? Doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t he know that I\uc1 \u8217 ?m like a child and there are situations where I just let everything go out from under me? And then, God forgive me, I thought I\uc1 \u8217 ?d never have moment\uc1 \u8217 ?s relaxation. Even a puppet made of steel would get worn out if the strings were pulled from morning to night and from night until morning. I must relieve them of their boredom\uc1 \u8212 ?I take that for granted\uc1 \u8212 ?but I have to amuse myself sometimes. In the middle of this mess, a fatal thought went through my mind, an idea which made me arrogant and inspired me with pride and insolence: it was the notion that they couldn\uc1 \u8217 ?t do without me, that I was someone indispensable.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Yes, I think you\uc1 \u8217 ?re very useful to them, but they\uc1 \u8217 ?re even more so to you. You won\uc1 \u8217 ?t find a house as good as that one, when you want to, but those people, if they\uc1 \u8217 ?re missing one fool, can come up with a hundred.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 A hundred fools like me! Monsieur Philosopher, they\uc1 \u8217 ?re not as common as that. Yes, some insipid fools. It\uc1 \u8217 ?s harder to find quality in foolishness than in talent or virtue. I\uc1 \u8217 ?m a rarity of my species, yes, very rare. Now that they don\uc1 \u8217 ?t have me anymore, what are they doing? They\uc1 \u8217 ?re as bored as dogs. I\uc1 \u8217 ?m an inexhaustible sack of impertinence. At every moment I had a joke which made people laugh until they cried. For them I was an entire madhouse.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 So that\uc1 \u8217 ?s why you had table, bed, coat, vest, trousers, shoes, and one pistole per month.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Pistole: the name of a large gold coin (the Louis d\uc1 \u8217 ?Or), perhaps worth two or three hundred dollars in today\uc1 \u8217 ?s money.}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Well, that\uc1 \u8217 ?s the good side. That\uc1 \u8217 ?s the income. But what about the expenses? You don\uc1 \u8217 ?t say a word about those. First, if there was a rumour about a new play, no matter what the weather, I had to poke my nose in all the attics in Paris until I found the author. Then I had to find a way to read the work and to insinuate skilfully that there was }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 a role}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  in it which would be performed extremely well by someone I knew. \uc1 \u8220 ?By whom, if you please?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?By whom\uc1 \u8212 ?a good question! Someone with grace, charm, and delicacy.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?You mean Mademoiselle Dangeville? Do you know her by any chance?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Yes, a little. But it\uc1 \u8217 ?s not her.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Then who?\uc1 \u8221 ? I\uc1 \u8217 ?d say her name in a low voice. \uc1 \u8220 ?Her!\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Yes, her,\uc1 \u8221 ? I\uc1 \u8217 ?d repeat, somewhat ashamed, for there are times I feel a sense of shame, and when I repeated the name you should\uc1 \u8217 ?ve seen the poet make a long face or at other times burst out laughing right in front of me. However, for better or worse I had to bring my man to dinner\uc1 \u8212 ?and he was afraid of getting involved. He\uc1 \u8217 ?d stall and offer his thanks. You should\uc1 \u8217 ?ve seen how I was treated if I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t succeed in my negotiations with him: I was a lout, a fool, an oaf. I was good for nothing. I wasn\uc1 \u8217 ?t worth the glass of water they\uc1 \u8217 ?d given