e, for self-interested souls\uc1 \u8212 ?vile and two-timing? If they understand us, then everything\uc1 \u8217 ?s fine. There is a tacit agreement that they\uc1 \u8217 ?ll provide good things for us and sooner or later we\uc1 \u8217 ?ll pay back the good they\uc1 \u8217 ?ve done us with something bad. Isn\uc1 \u8217 ?t this the agreement that exists between a man and his pet monkey or parrot? Brun is outraged that Palissot, his dinner companion and friend, has written some couplets attacking him. Palissot was bound to compose the couplets, and it\uc1 \u8217 ?s Brun who\uc1 \u8217 ?s in the wrong. Poinsinet is outraged that Palissot has ascribed to him the couplets he wrote against Brun. But Palissot was bound to ascribe to Poinsinet the couplets he wrote attacking Brun, and it\uc1 \u8217 ?s Poinsinet who\uc1 \u8217 ?s in the wrong. The little Abb\uc1 \u233 ? Rey is outraged that his friend Palissot has snatched away his mistress after he introduced her to him. But he shouldn\uc1 \u8217 ?t have introduced someone like Palissot to his mistress if he wasn\uc1 \u8217 ?t prepared to lose her. Palissot did his duty, and it\uc1 \u8217 ?s Abb\uc1 \u233 ? Rey who is in the wrong. The bookseller David is outraged because his associate Palissot has slept }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 with,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  or wanted to sleep }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 with,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  his wife. The wife of the bookseller David is outraged that Palissot has told anyone willing to listen that he has slept with her. Whether Palissot has slept with the bookseller\uc1 \u8217 ?s wife or not is difficult to determine, because the wife was bound to deny the fact and Palissot could have let people believe what was not true. Whatever the case, Palissot played his role, and it\uc1 \u8217 ?s David and his wife who are in the wrong. Helv\uc1 \u233 ?tius may be outraged that Palissot slanders him by putting him in a scene of a play as a dishonest man while Palissot still owes him the money he borrowed for the medical treatment for his bad health, as well as for food and clothing. But should Helv\uc1 \u233 ?tius have expected any other treatment from a man soiled with all sorts of infamy, a man }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 who,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  for }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 fun,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  makes his friend swear off his religion, who appropriates the assets of his partners, who has no faith, law, or feeling, who runs after fortune }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 per fas et nefas [through right and wrong]}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , who measures his days by the acts of villainy he commits, and who has even lampooned himself on stage as one of the most dangerous rascals\uc1 \u8212 ?a piece of impudence which I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t believe we}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8217 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ve seen an example of in the past and won\uc1 \u8217 ?t see in the future? No. So it\uc1 \u8217 ?s not Palissot but Helv\uc1 \u233 ?tius who\uc1 \u8217 ?s in the wrong. If one takes a young man from the provinces to the zoo at Versailles and his foolishness persuades him to stick his hand through the bars of the tiger\uc1 \u8217 ?s or panther\uc1 \u8217 ?s cage, and if the young man leaves his arm behind in the throat of the ferocious animal, who\uc1 \u8217 ?s in the wrong? All that is written in the tacit agreement. Too bad for the man who doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t know that or forgets it. How many of those accused of viciousness }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 could I}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  justify by appealing to this universal and sacred pact}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ? Instead}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  of accusing }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 them,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  people should accuse themselves of stupidity. Yes, you fat countess, you\uc1 \u8217 ?re the one in the wrong when you gather around you what people of your sort call \uc1 \u8220 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 characters,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \uc1 \u8221 ? and when these \uc1 \u8220 ?characters\uc1 \u8221 ? play dirty tricks on you and make you do the same, thus exposing you to the resentment of decent people. Respectable people do what they ought to do, so do your \uc1 \u8220 ?characters.\uc1 \u8221 ? And it\uc1 \u8217 ?s your fault for having collected them. If Bertinhus lived quietly and peacefully with his mistress, if through the probity of their }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 characters,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  they\uc1 \u8217 ?d made the acquaintance of decent people, if they\uc1 \u8217 ?d summoned round them men of talent and people known in society for their virtue, if they\uc1 \u8217 ?d reserved for a small, enlightened, select group hours of entertainment taken from the sweet life they had together, loving each other and telling each other so in the quiet of their retreat, do you think people would have made up stories about them, good or bad? So then what happened to them? They got what they deserved. They\uc1 \u8217 ?ve been punished for their imprudence. And we\uc1 \u8217 ?re the ones whom Providence has destined from all eternity to bring justice to the Bertins of today. And it\uc1 \u8217 ?s people like us among our descendants who are destined to bring justice to the Montsauges and Bertins of the future. But while we execute Providence\uc1 \u8217 ?s just decrees against stupidity, you paint us as we are and carry out her just decrees against us. What would you think of us, if, with our disgraceful habits, we claimed that we enjoyed popular favour? You\uc1 \u8217 ?d say we were out of our minds. And those who expect decent treatment from people born vicious, from vile and base characters, are they wise? Everything in this world receives its due. There are two public prosecutors. The one waiting by your door punishes the criminal offences against society. Nature is the other. She recognizes all the vices which escape the laws. You devote yourself to debauchery with women\uc1 \u8212 ?you\uc1 \u8217 ?ll get dropsy. You\uc1 \u8217 ?re a scoundrel\uc1 \u8212 ?you\uc1 \u8217 ?ll get consumption. You open your door to rascals and live with them\uc1 \u8212 ?you\uc1 \u8217 ?ll be betrayed, mocked, and despised. The simplest thing to do is resign yourself to the equity of these judgments and tell yourself that it\uc1 \u8217 ?s appropriate. Then you can rouse yourself to change your ways, or else stay as you are, but on the conditions mentioned above.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 You\uc1 \u8217 ?re right.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 In fact, about these bad stories\uc1 \u8212 ?I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t myself make any of them up. I stick to the role of peddler. They say that a few days ago, at five o\uc1 \u8217 ?clock in the morning, people could hear a r