lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Instead of answering me, he began to shake his head. Then, raising his finger to the sky he added, \uc1 \u8220 ?The star! The star! When nature made Leo, Vinci, Pergolese, and Duni, she smiled. She assumed an imposing and serious expression when she formed my dear uncle Rameau, whom people will call the Great Rameau for ten years and then, in a little while, won\uc1 \u8217 ?t mention any more. When nature did up his nephew, she made grimace after grimace, and then grimaced again.\uc1 \u8221 ? While he uttered these words, he made all sorts of faces\uc1 \u8212 ?disgust, disdain, irony\uc1 \u8212 ?and he seemed to be kneading in his fingers a piece of dough and smiling at the ridiculous shapes he made with it. This done, he threw the misshapen idol far away from him and said, \uc1 \u8220 ?That\uc1 \u8217 ?s how nature made me and threw me away, alongside other idols, some with wrinkled fat stomachs, short necks, huge eyes outside their heads, apoplectic, others with scrawny necks, wizened, with a sharp eye and a hooked nose. All of them started to burst out laughing when they saw me. And I put my two fists against my sides and exploded with laughter when I saw them, for fools and madmen amuse each other. They seek each other out. They attract each other. If, on my arrival there, I hadn\uc1 \u8217 ?t found }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \