hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 And you think I haven\uc1 \u8217 ?t tried. I wasn\uc1 \u8217 ?t fifteen years old when I first said to myself, \uc1 \u8220 ?What are you up to, Rameau? You\uc1 \u8217 ?re dreaming. And what are you dreaming about? That you\uc1 \u8217 ?d like to have done or do something which excites the admiration of the universe. Well, then, you just have to blow on your fingers and wiggle them. Just get started, and you\uc1 \u8217 ?ll be there.\uc1 \u8221 ? At a more advanced age, I repeated what I\uc1 \u8217 ?d said to myself in my childhood. Today, I\uc1 \u8217 ?m still repeating it, and I\uc1 \u8217 ?m standing by the statue of Memnon.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 The statue of the pharaoh Amenhotep III in Egypt gave out sounds each morning as the sun warmed the stone. Greeks and Romans who visited the statue called it Memnon after a Trojan hero who sang to his mother (the goddess of dawn).}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 What do you mean talking about the statue of Memnon?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 That\uc1 \u8217 ?s obvious enough, it seems to me. Around the statue of Memnon there were numberless other statues which the sun\uc1 \u8217 ?s rays struck just as much, but Memnon\uc1 \u8217 ?s statue was the only one which produced a sound. Who\uc1 \u8217 ?s a poet? Well, there\uc1 \u8217 ?s Voltaire. And who else? Voltaire. And a third? Voltaire. And a fourth? Voltaire. And musicians? There\uc1 \u8217 ?s Rinaldo da Capua, Hasse, Pergolesi, Alberti, Tartini, Locatelli, Terradoglias; there\uc1 \u8217 ?s my uncle, and little Duni, who\uc1 \u8217 ?s nothing to look at, no figure, but who feels, my God, who has melody and expression. The others around this small number of Memnons are just so many pairs of ears stuck on the end of sticks. And so we\uc1 \u8217 ?re beggars, so poor it\uc1 \u8217 ?s a miracle. O Monsieur Philosopher, poverty is a terrible thing. I see her crouching there, her mouth gaping open to receive a few drops of icy cold water dripping from the barrel of the Danaids.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 The Danaids in Greek mythology were the daughters of Danaus, punished for killing their husbands. In Hades they had to keep trying to fill leaky jars with water.}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  I don\uc1 \u8217 ?t know if she sharpens the mind of the philosopher, but she has a devilish way of cooling off the head of a poet. People don\uc1 \u8217 ?t sing well under this barrel. But the man who can get himself under it is only too lucky. I was there, and I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t know how to keep my place. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d already done that stupid thing once before. I\uc1 \u8217 ?d been traveling in Bohemia, Germany, Switzerland, Holland, Flanders, all over the damned place.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Under the leaky barrel.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Yes, under the leaky barrel. The man was a rich Jew who was happy to splash his money around. He liked music and my silly jokes. I played music in the way that made God happy\uc1 \u8212 ?and I played the fool. I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t lack anything. My Jew was a man who understood his law and who observed it strictly in every detail, sometimes with a friend, always with strangers. He got himself }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 into}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  bad }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 trouble,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  which I must tell you about, because it\uc1 \u8217 ?s amusing. In Utrecht there was a charming prostitute. He was attracted to this Christian and sent her a messenger with quite a large letter of credit. The strange creature rejected his offer. The Jew grew desperate. The messenger told him, \uc1 \u8220 ?Why are you so upset by this? You want to sleep with a good-looking woman. Nothing is easier, even to sleep with one more beautiful than the one you\uc1 \u8217 ?re chasing. That\uc1 \u8217 ?s my wife. I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll let you have her for the same price.\uc1 \u8221 ? No sooner said than done. The messenger keeps the letter of credit, and my Jew sleeps with the messenger\uc1 \u8217 ?s wife. The due date for the letter of credit arrives. The Jew allows the letter to be challenged and disputes its validity. A legal proceeding. The Jew tells himself, \uc1 \u8220 ?The man will never dare to reveal what right he has to possess my letter, and I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll not have to pay him.\uc1 \u8221 ? At the hearing, he interrogates the messenger, \uc1 \u8220 ?This letter of credit, who did you get it from?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?From you.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Is it for a loan?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?No.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Is it for the sale of merchandise?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?No.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?Is it for services rendered?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?No, but that\uc1 \u8217 ?s not the point. I\uc1 \u8217 ?m in possession of the letter. You signed it, and you will discharge it.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t sign it.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?So then I\uc1 \u8217 ?m a forger?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?You or someone else you\uc1 \u8217 ?re acting for.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?I\uc1 \u8217 ?m a coward, but you\uc1 \u8217 ?re a scoundrel. Believe me, don\uc1 \u8217 ?t push me to the limit. I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll tell everything. I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll dishonour myself, but I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll sink you.\uc1 \u8221 ? The Jew paid no attention to the threat, and at the next hearing the messenger revealed the entire affair. They were both reprimanded, and the Jew was condemned to pay off the letter of credit, and the money was applied to the relief of the poor. At that point I left him and came back here. What was I to do? I had to do something or die of poverty. All sorts of plans went through my head. One day, I was going to leave tomorrow to join up with a troupe travelling through the provinces\uc1 \u8212 ?I\uc1 \u8217 ?d be equally good or bad in the theatre or the orchestra. The next day, I was dreaming of getting someone to paint for me one of those pictures attached to a pole which people set up at a public crossroad, where I\uc1 \u8217 ?d have shouted my head off, \uc1 \u8220 ?Here\uc1 \u8217 ?s the town where he was born. Here he is leaving his father the apothecary. Here he is arriving in the capital, looking for his uncle\uc1 \u8217 ?s residence. Here he is on his knees before his uncle, who is chasing him away. Here he is with a Jew,\uc1 \u8221 ? and so on and so on. The next day, I\uc1 \u8217 ?d get up firmly resolved to join up with the street singers. That\uc1 \u8217 ?s not the worst thing I could\uc1 \u8217 ?ve done. We could have gone to give a concert under my dear uncle\uc1 \u8217 ?s windows. He\uc1 \u8217 ?d have collapsed with rage. But I chose something else.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 At that }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 point,}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  he stopped and assumed, in succession, the pose of a man holding a violin and turning his wrist to tighten the strings, then the pose of a poor devil worn out with exhaustion, with no energy and wobbling limbs, ready to die if someone didn\uc1 \u8217 ?t throw him a piece of bread. He showed his extreme need with the gesture of a finger pointing towards his half-open mouth. Then he added, \uc1 \u8220 ?You see what I mean. They\uc1 \u8217 ?d toss me the loaf, and three or four of us, all famished, would fight over it. So go on, then\uc1 \u8212 ?think grand thoughts, create beautiful things in an environment of such distress.\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 That\uc1 \u8217 ?s difficult.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 From one tumble to the next\uc1 \u8212 ?I fell into that job. I was in clover. Now I\uc1 \u8217 ?ve left it. Now I\uc1 \u8217 ?ll have to scrape the gut once again and come back to that gesture with my finger pointing at my gaping mouth. Nothing\uc1 \u8217 ?s stable in this world. Today at the top of the wheel, tomorrow at the bottom. Damned circumstances lead us along and lead us really badly.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Then, drinking up what remained at the bottom of the bottle, he spoke to the man next to him: \uc1 \u8220 ?Sir, would you be so good as to give me a pinch of snuff}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  That\uc1 \u8217 ?s a lovely box you have there. Are you a musician?\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?No.\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?All the better for you, for they\uc1 \u8217 ?re poor buggers, a pitiful bunch. Destiny wanted me to be a musician, while in a mill in Montmartre there\uc1 \u8217 ?s perhaps a miller or a miller\uc1 \u8217 ?s helper who\uc1 \u8217 ?ll never listen to anything but the sound of the ratchet and who\uc1 \u8217 ?d have made up some fine songs. Rameau, go to the mill\uc1 \u8212 ?to the mill\uc1 \u8212 ?that\uc1 \u8217 ?s where you belong.\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 ME}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Whatever a man devotes himself to, that\uc1 \u8217 ?s what nature has destined him to do.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 HIM}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 She makes some strange mistakes. In my case, I\uc1 \u8217 ?m not looking down from that height where everything merges into one\uc1 \u8212 ?where the man who prunes a tree with cutters and the caterpillar who eats the leaves seem nothing but two different insects, each doing his own work. Go and perch on the epicycle of Mercury and from there, like R\uc1 \u233 ?aumur, who classifies flies into seamstresses, surveyors, and harvesters, you can, if you like, divide up the human species into woodworkers, carpenters, roofers, dancers, singers\uc1 \u8212 ?whatever you want.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sa60 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Ren\uc1 \u233 ? de R\uc1 \u233 ?amur (1683-1757): French natural philosopher noted for his work on insects.}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  I won\uc1 \u8217 ?t get involved in it. I\uc1 \u8217 ?m in the world, and I\uc1 \u8217 ?m staying here. But if it\uc1 \u8217 ?s part of nature to have an appetite\uc1 \u8212 ?for it\uc1 \u8217 ?s always appetite I come back to, to the feeling which is always present in me\uc1 \u8212 ?I find that it\uc1 \u8217 ?s not part of a good order if one doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t always have something to eat. It\uc1 \u8217 ?s a damnable economy with men who cram themselves with everything while others whose stomachs are just as demanding as theirs and have a recurring hunger like theirs have nothing to chew on. The worst thing is the way our need compels us to a certain posture. The man in need doesn\uc1 \u8217 ?t walk like another man\uc1 \u8212 ?he jumps, he grovels, he wriggles, he crawls. He spends his life taking up and carrying out various positions.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin480 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \fi-480 \cufi-200 \li480 \ri0